  "heading": "\\dedekind.from.cauchy(x_)",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Dedekind cut of a Cauchy real}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\dedekind.from.cauchy(x_)]\nDefines: cut(x_) is \\(bijective)::function:on{\\real.cauchy.carrier}:to{\\dedekind.cut.carrier}\nexpresses:\n. forAll: A ::= a(n_) ::= qa_ is \\cauchy.rational.sequence\n  then:\n  . forAll: q is \\rational\n    then:\n    . let: C is \\dedekind.cut\n      where: C = cut(\\real.cauchy.class:of{A})\n      then:\n      . have: q \"in\"? C\n        iff:\n        . exists: epsilon is \\rational\n          suchThat:\n          . \\rational.zero \\:rational.less?:/ epsilon\n          . exists: N is \\natural\n            suchThat:\n            . forAll: n is \\natural\n              where: N \\:natural.leq?:/ n\n              then:\n              . let: r is \\rational\n                where: r = q \\.rational.+./ epsilon\n                then:\n                . let: s is \\rational\n                  where: s = a(n)\n                  then: r \\:rational.less?:/ s\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Dedekind cut of a Cauchy real\"\n. description: \"The canonical bijection sending a Cauchy-real class to the lower\n                set of rationals that remain a positive rational distance below\n                a representative sequence.\"\nId: \"28fd2c5f-4aec-46ad-bdfe-557bd5e0a157\"",
